# Cursor Rules — Dr. Ahmed Mazen Website

Always read CLAUDE.md before writing any code. It contains the full project brief.

## Identity
- Client: Dr. Ahmed Mazen, aesthetic medicine consultant, Cairo Egypt
- Stack: Vanilla HTML + CSS + JS, no frameworks
- Languages: Arabic (primary, RTL) + English (secondary, LTR toggle)

## Design Rules
- Background: #0A0A0A (black). Accent: #C9A84C (gold). Text: #F5F0E8 (off-white)
- Use CSS variables only — never hardcode colors
- Fonts: Cairo (Arabic), Playfair Display / Montserrat (English), loaded via Google Fonts

## Code Rules
- Every text string = `<span class="ar-text">...</span><span class="en-text">...</span>`
- Primary CTA = WhatsApp link to https://wa.me/201274477111
- All images use `loading="lazy"` below the fold
- No jQuery, no React, no Vue — pure vanilla JS
- Animations via CSS transitions (0.3s ease) and IntersectionObserver
- Mobile-first CSS with breakpoints at 480px, 768px, 1024px

## SEO Rules
- Title format: `[Arabic Service Name] | دكتور أحمد مازن`
- Meta description: 150-160 chars, include primary Arabic keyword
- Each service page needs Schema.org MedicalProcedure JSON-LD
- Internal links from every page back to homepage

## New Pages
When creating service pages, follow the template in CLAUDE.md:
Hero → Description → How it works → Before/After → FAQ → CTA → Related services → Footer

When creating blog articles, target Arabic search terms like:
"أفضل دكتور فيلر في مصر", "شد الوجه بدون جراحة", "الفرق بين الفيلر والبوتكس"
